{# The Speed view: the same search against a plain ILIKE, then the benchmark of nine queries on demand. #}
<div class="stack">
    {% if result and result.hits %}
        {# The page shows this search's own time at once; the comparison (the warm median of both sides) is measured by its own request. #}
        <div class="speed-bars" data-controller="ilike" data-src="{{ path('search_ilike', {q: q, cat: category ?: null, stock: stock is null ? null : (stock ? 1 : 0), ay: asYouType ? 1 : 0}) }}">
            <div class="busy-region" data-ilike-target="region" data-loading-message="Measuring both sides…" aria-busy="true">
                <div class="speed-row">
                    <span>Fuzzphony</span>
                    <span class="speed-bar"><span class="is-fuzzphony" style="width: 2%"></span></span>
                    <span class="speed-value">{{ result.tookMs < 10 ? result.tookMs|number_format(1) : result.tookMs|number_format(0) }} ms</span>
                </div>
                <div class="speed-row">
                    <span>ILIKE</span>
                    <span class="speed-bar"><span class="skeleton" style="width: 100%; height: 100%"></span></span>
                    <span class="speed-value muted">scanning {{ rowEstimate > 0 ? rowEstimate|number_format : 'the catalogue' }} rows…</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="muted">The first figure is this search, as it was just run. The bars replace it with the warm median of {{ warmRuns }} runs after one cold run, for the search without its facets, and ILIKE is measured the same way, in a request of its own so this page never waits for it. <code>ILIKE '%…%'</code> does not rank, fold accents, stem or tolerate typos.</p>
    {% else %}
        <div class="empty"><strong>Nothing to compare yet</strong>Search something that finds products, then see how long it takes next to a plain <code>ILIKE</code>.</div>
    {% endif %}

    <ul class="list">
        <li class="row no-lead">
            <div class="row-body">
                <div class="row-title">The benchmark</div>
                <div class="row-sub">Nine queries, one after the other, on {{ rowEstimate > 0 ? rowEstimate|number_format ~ ' products' : 'the catalogue' }}.</div>
            </div>
            <a class="button" href="{{ path('benchmark') }}" data-loading-message="Opening the benchmark…">Open</a>
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>
